"1787567028354410001-ea7221dc-d1aa-4c13-9a7b-0538b7b0dd8c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"78cf9807eb2ed39dec773870a16ec2850932a892b58a510ddfe799e8db73bc44","event_uuid":"4aa2fe65-8f62-4a05-bb25-26d49714a327","position":{"commit_sha":"cddb4594308579ea0798e5bea12cac90e17df1bd","position":"1787567363685737001-4aa2fe65-8f62-4a05-bb25-26d49714a327"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"385c6627ec5a6c7a573bef71cb42d8ebe8c72397d6c2f0dd0d90f2085f69f8ed","event_uuid":"eb2d8092-a78a-4a99-9ed1-30a8f852b882","position":{"commit_sha":"52aa20a70c70ed7f25cf2dbed7d376edbb7a566f","position":"1787567381194474001-eb2d8092-a78a-4a99-9ed1-30a8f852b882"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787462410526395001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c9fd2f49-9bdc-4a92-b64c-ef31a42f05aa","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"65c9-aba3-c744-483a"},{"link_uuid":"1c4bc204-7bef-4aa5-b976-061b731e5445","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c68f-9af1-a6b2-4c5d"},{"link_uuid":"9ea84cfd-feae-4af8-898a-8664e29c316f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"aa3e-311c-9d7b-4e99"}],"description":"## Context\nF12 (story 65c9, \"Complete registry-backed CLI help discovery\") committed one help artifact for every visible route that is not retired and generates the CLI reference from those artifacts. Manual review found writing-guideline violations in the help that F12 newly exposed. The affected output inherits parser descriptions and option help strings that predate the documentation policy. Violations occur in help for `verify-completion`, `sign-review`, `explain`, `review-plan`, `review-code`, `scan-spec`, `verify-identity`, `verify-authorship`, `verify-opcert`, `verify-commit-ticket`, `enrich`, `trusted-env`, and `remote-cert`, and in the aggregated `overview.txt` summaries. F08A and F10 do not provide general coverage for parser-owned CLI help. The operator rejected character restrictions and other mechanical prose enforcement.\n\nThe writing rules that the affected text breaks are defined in `docs/documentation-policy.md` under \"Writing rules\": no em dash or en dash, no semicolon, no clause-joining colon, no spaced-hyphen connector used as a dash, formal complete sentences for an external audience, and the banned-word list.\n\n## Scope\nThe scope is exactly the parser-owned help that F12 newly committed (the 21 artifacts added in commit `131e75a`) that carries a violation, corrected at the maintained parser source, plus the two generated projections (`overview.txt` and `docs/cli-reference.md`). Help that predates F12 and was already exposed is out of scope. Usage strings, metavar tokens, option flag names, exit codes, and configuration keys are technical identifiers and stay byte-for-byte unchanged.\n\n## Source-to-artifact trace\nEach violating generated line is corrected at its maintained source:\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/llm.py` owns the descriptions and option help for `review-code`, `scan-spec`, `verify-completion`, `explain`, `review-plan`, `sign-review`, and the shared `_add_ref_source` helper (`--ref` / `--source`).\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/verify.py` owns `verify-opcert`, `verify-identity` / `verify-authorship`, and `verify-commit-ticket`.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/enrich.py` owns the `enrich` `mode` help.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/certs.py` owns the `trusted-env` positional and `--root` help.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/remote_cert.py` module docstring is used verbatim as the `remote-cert` description.\nThe committed `src/rebar/_cli/help/*.txt` artifacts and `docs/cli-reference.md` are regenerated from these sources by the existing generators; they are never hand-edited.\n\n## Implementation plan\n1. Rewrite the parser descriptions and option help strings above for an external user audience: replace em/en dashes and clause-joining colons with complete sentences, remove semicolons, remove banned words and all-caps emphasis padding, and keep each Markdown/paragraph line as one logical line. Preserve command meaning, argparse behavior, technical identifiers, config keys, flag names, and exit codes exactly.\n2. Regenerate the committed help with `python scripts/gen_cli_help.py` and the CLI reference with `python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py`.\n3. Verify no drift with `python scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check` and `python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py --check`.\n\n## Testing approach\nPortability: all validation runs through repository scripts and pytest with no dependency on any specific CI provider.\n- The existing drift checks (`scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check`, `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py --check`, and `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_help.py`) prove the committed artifacts stay byte-current with the parser sources after the rewrite.\n- Add one focused content-specific contract test, `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_help_writing_guidelines_jerboa.py`, that asserts the specific corrected wording of the affected commands (positive assertions on the rewritten phrasing plus the absence of the exact constructs that were removed from those named commands). This is a narrow behavior test over the affected commands, not a repository-wide character gate, banned-word scanner, or punctuation scanner.\n\nNo mechanical character or prose enforcement gate is introduced.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The affected committed help and CLI reference prose conforms to the project writing guidelines.\n- [x] Each changed generated line is corrected at its maintained parser source.\n- [x] Command semantics, syntax, technical identifiers, and exit behavior remain unchanged.\n- [x] The help and CLI-reference drift checks pass (`gen_cli_help.py --check`, `gen_cli_reference.py --check`).\n- [x] Focused CLI help contracts pass.\n- [x] No mechanical character or prose enforcement is introduced.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/llm.py","reason":"Rewrite parser descriptions and option help for verify-completion, sign-review, review-plan, review-code, scan-spec, explain, and the shared --ref/--source helper to conform to writing guidelines (remove em/en dashes, semicolons, clause-joining colons, banned words) for an external audience."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/verify.py","reason":"Rewrite verify-opcert, verify-identity/verify-authorship, and verify-commit-ticket descriptions and option help; remove semicolons and clause-joining colons."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/enrich.py","reason":"Rewrite the enrich mode option help to remove the clause-joining semicolon."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/certs.py","reason":"Rewrite trusted-env target/--root option help to remove semicolons."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/remote_cert.py","reason":"Rewrite the module docstring used as the remote-cert CLI description to remove em dashes and a clause-joining colon."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/verify-completion.txt","reason":"Regenerated help artifact."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/sign-review.txt","reason":"Regenerated help artifact."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/review-plan.txt","reason":"Regenerated help artifact."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/review-code.txt","reason":"Regenerated help artifact."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/scan-spec.txt","reason":"Regenerated help artifact."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/explain.txt","reason":"Regenerated help artifact."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/verify-opcert.txt","reason":"Regenerated help artifact."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/verify-identity.txt","reason":"Regenerated help artifact."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/verify-authorship.txt","reason":"Regenerated help artifact."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/verify-commit-ticket.txt","reason":"Regenerated help artifact."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/enrich.txt","reason":"Regenerated help artifact."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/trusted-env.txt","reason":"Regenerated help artifact."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/remote-cert.txt","reason":"Regenerated help artifact."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/overview.txt","reason":"Regenerated overview summaries derived from parser descriptions."},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"Regenerated CLI reference embedding the corrected committed help."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_help_writing_guidelines_jerboa.py","reason":"New content-specific contract test asserting the corrected wording of the affected command help (positive assertions on rewritten phrasing), not a mechanical repo-wide scanner."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py","reason":"Update the existing review-plan retry help assertion to the corrected lower-case wording."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","aa3e-311c-9d7b-4e99"],["relates_to","c68f-9af1-a6b2-4c5d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"4aa2fe65-8f62-4a05-bb25-26d49714a327","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["documentation","proposal","cli"],"ticket_id":"5b4f-2072-3057-4dfe","ticket_type":"task","title":"F20 align generated CLI help with documentation writing guidelines","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e83f6370-75de